WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.480
Big questions. A clearer view of what comes next. This

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.310
is Chooch AI.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.950
What if your shelves could tell you what they need?

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:13.103
Chooch AI turns shelf images into approximate inventory counts—using the

00:00:13.103 --> 00:00:17.824
shelves you already have, without barcode scans or RFID tags.

00:00:18.374 --> 00:00:23.652
When stock runs low, replenishment signals follow. Real-time visibility replaces

00:00:23.652 --> 00:00:25.104
yesterday’s guesswork.

00:00:25.654 --> 00:00:28.864
Can visibility scale without compromising privacy?

00:00:29.444 --> 00:00:34.671
No patient data is captured; identifying features are blurred on-device.

00:00:34.671 --> 00:00:38.374
Chooch is HIPAA compliant, ISO and SOC 2 certified.

00:00:38.924 --> 00:00:44.370
Gartner’s May 2026 report describes a rollout across seventeen hundred

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.405
inventory rooms in forty-one hospitals.

00:00:47.955 --> 00:00:51.095
What if service meant availability—not just delivery?

00:00:51.675 --> 00:00:56.657
Picture demand based on actual use. Distributors can consolidate orders

00:00:56.657 --> 00:00:59.184
and plan fewer emergency deliveries.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:04.094
Managed inventory can then reach hundreds of rooms without expanding

00:01:04.094 --> 00:01:05.504
manual counting teams.

00:01:06.054 --> 00:01:07.764
What could your teams do with time back?

00:01:08.344 --> 00:01:13.253
Reported deployments show up to fifty percent higher supply-chain productivity

00:01:13.253 --> 00:01:16.274
and up to forty-to-fifty percent less inventory.

00:01:16.824 --> 00:01:21.512
Critical stockouts fall by up to ninety-five percent; expiration waste

00:01:21.512 --> 00:01:24.994
by around fifteen percent. Results vary by facility.

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:28.004
Why wait for an empty shelf to sound the alarm?

00:01:28.584 --> 00:01:32.948
Resilience starts with knowing what you have. Live consumption trends

00:01:32.948 --> 00:01:36.364
warn of shortages before shelves empty—even overnight.

00:01:36.914 --> 00:01:42.108
Teams can redistribute supplies, source alternatives and locate recalled products

00:01:42.108 --> 00:01:43.904
with a recorded audit trail.

00:01:44.454 --> 00:01:47.394
What changes when both sides see the same reality?

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:53.301
Now the conversation changes: anticipate seasonal demand, agree on substitutes,

00:01:53.301 --> 00:01:57.144
and measure success by availability at the point of care.

00:01:57.694 --> 00:02:01.339
Shared facts build trust—and a stronger basis for pricing and

00:02:01.339 --> 00:02:02.594
contract discussions.

00:02:03.144 --> 00:02:06.142
If inventory gets smarter, what stays in your hands?

00:02:06.722 --> 00:02:12.349
Your clinical routines, care decisions, ERP, purchasing contracts and approvals

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:15.341
stay yours. Chooch feeds existing systems.

00:02:15.891 --> 00:02:21.513
Supply-chain expertise shifts toward exceptions and planning. Less repetitive counting.

00:02:21.513 --> 00:02:22.871
More time for people.

00:02:23.421 --> 00:02:26.680
The right supplies. The right place. The right time. Chooch

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.061
AI. A healthier tomorrow.
